{
  "summary": "You have produced an outstanding report that achieved full marks across every criterion. Your ethical framing, stakeholder mapping, and balanced arguments were exceptionally thorough. You integrated authoritative case studies, qualitative and quantitative evidence, and clear visual aids to construct a compelling recommendation for Rachel and other key stakeholders. Maintaining this level of rigorous research, clear structure, and actionable decision-making will ensure continued success in future engineering case analyses.",
  "next_steps": [
    "Continue to use structured visual aids, such as Table 1 and Figure 1, to make multi-stakeholder decisions clear and accessible in future reports.",
    "Maintain your practice of combining quantitative data (e.g. costs and disruption metrics) with qualitative ethical codes to build persuasive technical arguments.",
    "Apply this systematic framework of balancing commercial constraints against safety-critical risks to complex, real-world engineering project proposals."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "You achieved the top rubric level by clearly framing ethical issues within engineering design cadences and organizational pressures. Table 1 effectively mapped each stakeholder's stakes and decision rights, fulfilling all criteria for 'Excellent'.",
    "C2": "Your discussion achieved 'Excellent' by objectively exploring arguments for and against shipping with great depth. In 'RECOMMENDATIONS', you provided distinct, actionable conclusions tailored to Rachel, management, and the health department.",
    "C3": "Your report maintained a compelling, highly structured argument. In 'The Most Ethical Path', you systematically balanced commercial benefits against non-consenting patient risk to fully justify your conclusion, meeting the 'Excellent' standard.",
    "C4": "You met the 'Excellent' requirements by substantiating claims with diverse case studies (e.g., WannaCry, Therac-25, Intel Pentium) alongside rigorous qualitative and quantitative evidence to illustrate the consequences of unmitigated defect risks.",
    "C5": "The report demonstrated 'Excellent' presentation, featuring fluent, professional language and proper IEEE references. Visual elements, such as your decision flowchart in Figure 1, were competently used to directly support the analysis."
  }
}
